ws a failure rather than the all-passed banner.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Update e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go to track package-level events and include them in report totals/output.\"},{\"title\":\"Scanner errors silently truncate the report input\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":79,\"endLine\":82,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":91,\"endLine\":113,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":152,\"endLine\":156,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"parseEvents uses bufio.Scanner with a 1 MiB token limit but never checks scanner.Err() after the loop. If a test output JSON line exceeds the limit, or the reader returns an I/O error, Scan stops and the function returns a partial parent list as if parsing succeeded. Later failing events can be omitted, producing a misleading report.\",\"reproduction\":\"Feed parseEvents a JSONL stream with an output event line larger than 1 MiB followed by a failing test event. Scanner stops with ErrTooLong before the failing event, but parseEvents returns normally with the failure missing.\",\"recommendation\":\"Make parseEvents return an error and check scanner.Err() after the scan loop. main should print the parse error and exit nonzero. Consider using json.Decoder or raising the scanner limit if large test output is expected.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The feature lists no linked tests, and no included test covers oversized JSON output or reader errors.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a parser test using a reader that triggers bufio.ErrTooLong and assert the command/reporting path returns an error instead of a partial successful report.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Change parseEvents and main in e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go to propagate and handle scanner errors.\"},{\"title\":\"Events 