{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:55:37.024Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"019e415e-ae61-7c12-bf74-6e6589dc1e58","last_agent_message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Package-level test failures are reported as all passed\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":91,\"endLine\":98,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":170,\"endLine\":181,\"symbol\":\"renderReport\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":245,\"endLine\":260,\"symbol\":\"renderReport\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"go test JSON uses events with an empty Test field for package-level failures such as build failures, TestMain/preflight exits, or package setup failures. parseEvents drops every event with ev.Test == \\\"\\\", so a JSON stream containing only a package-level fail produces no parents. renderReport then has failed == 0 and prints the success banner for zero tests. The wrapper may still exit nonzero, but the generated report artifact is materially wrong and can hide the actual failure cause from the report.\",\"reproduction\":\"Input JSONL: {\\\"Action\\\":\\\"fail\\\",\\\"Package\\\":\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/e2e/tests\\\",\\\"Elapsed\\\":0.1}\\\\n. parseEvents returns an empty parent list, and renderReport prints Total: 0 plus the all-passed footer.\",\"recommendation\":\"Preserve package-level fail/skip events instead of discarding them. Either render a package failure row keyed by Package or maintain a separate packageFailures section that contributes to the failed count and includes package output.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The feature lists no linked tests, and there is no evidence of a fixture that exercises JSON events with Action fail and an empty Test field.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a unit test for parseEvents/renderReport with a package-level fail event and no test-level events, asserting the report shows a failure rather than the all-passed banner.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Update e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go to track package-level events and include them in report totals/output.\"},{\"title\":\"Scanner errors silently truncate the report input\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":79,\"endLine\":82,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":91,\"endLine\":113,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":152,\"endLine\":156,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"parseEvents uses bufio.Scanner with a 1 MiB token limit but never checks scanner.Err() after the loop. If a test output JSON line exceeds the limit, or the reader returns an I/O error, Scan stops and the function returns a partial parent list as if parsing succeeded. Later failing events can be omitted, producing a misleading report.\",\"reproduction\":\"Feed parseEvents a JSONL stream with an output event line larger than 1 MiB followed by a failing test event. Scanner stops with ErrTooLong before the failing event, but parseEvents returns normally with the failure missing.\",\"recommendation\":\"Make parseEvents return an error and check scanner.Err() after the scan loop. main should print the parse error and exit nonzero. Consider using json.Decoder or raising the scanner limit if large test output is expected.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The feature lists no linked tests, and no included test covers oversized JSON output or reader errors.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a parser test using a reader that triggers bufio.ErrTooLong and assert the command/reporting path returns an error instead of a partial successful report.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Change parseEvents and main in e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go to propagate and handle scanner errors.\"},{\"title\":\"Events from different packages with the same test name are merged\",\"category\":\"api-contract\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":17,\"endLine\":23,\"symbol\":\"TestEvent\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":89,\"endLine\":104,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"startLine\":117,\"endLine\":141,\"symbol\":\"parseEvents\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"The parsed event type includes Package, but parseEvents keys the tests map only by ev.Test. In go test JSON, the unique test identity is package plus test name. If the command processes ./... output and two packages both have TestFoo, the later event stream overwrites or merges the earlier one, corrupting status, elapsed time, output, totals, and rerun guidance.\",\"reproduction\":\"Use JSONL with pass/fail events for Package \\\"a\\\" Test \\\"TestFoo\\\" and Package \\\"b\\\" Test \\\"TestFoo\\\". Only one map entry exists for TestFoo, so the report cannot represent both package results independently.\",\"recommendation\":\"Key parsed tests by both Package and Test, and render package context when more than one package is present. At minimum, include Package in the map key to prevent collisions.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The feature lists no linked tests, and no included fixture covers multiple packages containing the same test name.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a unit test with two JSON events sharing Test but using different Package values, asserting that both results appear independently in the report.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Update parseEvents in e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go to include Package in test identity and output grouping.\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"e2e/cmd/testreport/main.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/interactive/interactive.go\"],\"symbols\":[\"main\",\"openInput\",\"pars